&lt;p class=&quot;font-normal text-sm mb-4 last:mb-0 break-words&quot;&gt;At Man Group, we respect your privacy and we are committed to protecting and safeguarding your Personal Data. We have developed policies and processes which are designed to provide for the security and integrity of your Personal Data. We are committed to Processing your Personal Data fairly and lawfully, and being open and transparent about such Processing. For further information on how we process your data, please see the privacy notice for applicants&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;text-sm font-normal text-light-blue underline&quot; href=&quot;https://www.man.com/privacy-notice-job-applicant&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;* As at 31 March 2026&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Purpose of role:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Head of Stewardship, this role sits within the Stewardship team, which is part of the Responsible Investment group of Man Group. The candidate will focus on the implementation of stewardship approaches, including proxy voting and engagement across Man Group’s investment capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Specific responsibilities:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engagement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with portfolio managers and collaboratively with other investors to deliver tangible results at investee companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilise company disclosures, third party research and other available resources to conduct non-financial analysis to assess company adherence to ESG market standards across different industries, supporting junior team members in defining ESG best practice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify issuers for targeted engagement in order to meet our ESG / Responsible investment (RI) targets, prioritising based on materiality frameworks and strategic importance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead engagements with corporate representatives from our funds’ portfolio companies to discuss ESG matters, including climate change, biodiversity, human rights and corporate governance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting and Policy Updates&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the delivery of engagement and proxy voting-related queries in due diligence questionnaires (DDQ) or Requests for Information (RFI), ensuring consistency and quality of responses and coaching junior analysts in their contributions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the development and maintenance of stewardship-related policies and play a leading role in contributing to international stewardship codes’ requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Technical competencies:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A degree in finance, economics, business, law or other relevant subjects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional qualifications in finance or ESG, such as IMC, CFA level 1, CFA in ESG investing or other relevant qualification (desirable)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of policy issues of corporate governance, stewardship and shareholder rights and responsibilities, with evidence of knowledge of wider responsible investment issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong IT skills including proficiency with Microsoft Office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A motivated self-starter that is organised, structured and proactive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work collaboratively and independently, take initiative and add value to the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective communication and interpersonal skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation and writing skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented and analytical skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Information seeker and aptitude to problem-solving and holistic thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inclusion, Work-Life Balance and Benefits at Man Group&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll thrive in our working environment that champions equality of opportunity. Your unique perspective will contribute to our success, joining a workplace where inclusion is fundamental and deeply embedded in our culture and values. Through our external and internal initiatives, partnerships and programmes, you&#39;ll find opportunities to grow, develop your talents, and help foster an inclusive environment for all across our firm and industry. Learn more at &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.man.com/diversity&quot;&gt;www.man.com/diversity&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll have opportunities to make a difference through our charitable and global initiatives, while advancing your career through professional development, and with flexible working arrangements available too. Like all our people, you&#39;ll receive two annual &#39;Mankind&#39; days of paid leave for community volunteering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our comprehensive benefits package includes competitive holiday entitlements, pension/401k, life and long-term disability coverage, group sick pay, enhanced parental leave and long-service leave. Depending on your location, you may also enjoy additional benefits such as private medical coverage, discounted gym membership options and pet insurance.&lt;/p&gt;
